{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Hello, I'm Dr. Kenji Watanabe. Can I get your full name and date of birth, please?",
   "start": 0.08,
   "end": 5.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Priya Raghnathan, May 14th, 2002.",
   "start": 6.64,
   "end": 9.32
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thanks Priya, quite the rain out there today. Did you get soaked?",
   "start": 10.22,
   "end": 13.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A little, my umbrella flipped inside out on the way from the bus.",
   "start": 14.6,
   "end": 17.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Oh no, well, let's dry you off with some good news, hopefully. Your student health clinic sent you about palpitations.",
   "start": 18.64,
   "end": 25.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, for about three weeks I've been feeling this like fluttering in my chest, or like my heart skips and then does a big thump.",
   "start": 26.33,
   "end": 33.03
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "How long does each episode last?",
   "start": 33.79,
   "end": 35.65
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Just a few seconds. It happens a bunch of times a day, mostly at night when I'm lying in bed.",
   "start": 36.31,
   "end": 41.11
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Does it ever feel like a fast, steady racing that starts and stops suddenly?",
   "start": 41.73,
   "end": 46.59
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, not really racing, more like skipping.",
   "start": 47.39,
   "end": 49.43
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Have you fainted or felt like you were going to faint?",
   "start": 50.34,
   "end": 53.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, never.",
   "start": 54.06,
   "end": 54.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any chest pain or shortness of breath when it happens?",
   "start": 55.7,
   "end": 58.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Nope, it's just weird and it makes me anxious.",
   "start": 59.68,
   "end": 61.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That makes sense. Tell me about your caffeine. How much coffee or energy drinks are you having?",
   "start": 62.66,
   "end": 67.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Um, okay. So I'm in my second year of the pharmacy program at Lakeshore University, and finals prep has been rough. Probably four big cold brews a day, and then two energy drinks at night to keep studying. That's a lot of caffeine,",
   "start": 69.01,
   "end": 82.48
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "probably well over 1 ,000 milligrams a day. How much are you sleeping?",
   "start": 82.94,
   "end": 87.28
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Maybe five hours, sometimes less.",
   "start": 88.26,
   "end": 90.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any alcohol, vaping or other drugs?",
   "start": 91.05,
   "end": 93.75
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "A glass of wine on weekends sometimes. I don't smoke or vape.",
   "start": 94.37,
   "end": 97.89
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Medicines?",
   "start": 98.79,
   "end": 99.17
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Just my birth control pill once a day and I take melatonin 3 milligrams on nights I can't fall asleep. No allergies.",
   "start": 99.84,
   "end": 107.4
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any heart problems in the family or anyone who died suddenly when they were young?",
   "start": 108.5,
   "end": 113.34
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No heart stuff that I know of. My mom has a thyroid problem Hashimoto's she takes a pill for it.",
   "start": 114.16,
   "end": 119.68
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay good to know. Let me examine you. Blood pressure is 118 over 74 pulse 88 oxygen 99 percent. Your thyroid doesn't feel enlarged. No tremor in your hands. Heart has a regular rhythm. No murmurs or clicks. Lungs are clear.",
   "start": 120.74,
   "end": 137.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay.",
   "start": 138.5,
   "end": 138.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "We also did an ECG at check -in. It's a normal ECG, sinus rhythm at 84, with normal intervals and no signs of an extra electrical pathway.",
   "start": 139.86,
   "end": 151.0
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "So my heart is okay.",
   "start": 151.84,
   "end": 153.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Everything I'm seeing looks healthy. What you're describing sounds like extra beats, early beats from the top or bottom chambers which are very common and usually harmless. The big triggers are caffeine, energy drinks, and not enough sleep and you've got all three going on.",
   "start": 153.9,
   "end": 170.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yeah, that's fair.",
   "start": 170.98,
   "end": 171.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "So here's the plan. I'd like you to cut back the caffeine gradually over the next two weeks so you don't get withdrawal headaches. Aim for no more than one regular coffee a day and and no energy drinks at all, and try to get at least seven hours of sleep.",
   "start": 172.26,
   "end": 187.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "I can try. Finals end the 12th of December, so it'll get easier after that.",
   "start": 188.02,
   "end": 192.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Fair, I'm also ordering a thyroid test, a TSH, plus a blood count and electrolytes, just to rule out anything simple. If the palpitations are still happening in six weeks after you've cut back, we'll put a two -week patch monitor on you to record your rhythm.",
   "start": 192.96,
   "end": 209.46
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, what number do you have for me? I changed phones.",
   "start": 209.46,
   "end": 212.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I have 555 -0117.",
   "start": 213.66,
   "end": 216.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That's still right.",
   "start": 217.2,
   "end": 218.02
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good, if you ever faint, or have chest pain with the fluttering, or a racing heartbeat that won't stop, go to the emergency room. Otherwise, I'll see you back in six weeks.",
   "start": 218.68,
   "end": 229.36
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thank you, that's a relief honestly.",
   "start": 230.14,
   "end": 231.76
  }
 ],
